  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The parabola is written in vertex form, \n\n$$\ny=a(x-h)^{2}+k,\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ is the leading coefficient and $(h,k)$ is the vertex. \n\n- Since $h=16$ and $k=17,$ the vertex is $(16,17).$\n\n- Since $a=1>0,$ the parabola opens upwards.\n\nBecause the parabola opens upwards, there is no maximum output, and the vertex corresponds to the minimum output. \n\nTherefore, the range is $[17,\\infty ).$\n\nThe corresponding diagram is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14253498/assets/ef4e0bbd902f2904316c5a9db094b85ec8942c045020434171b9616077e6e3a3.png)",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
